{
  "id": "count-square-submatrices-with-all-ones",
  "questionId": "count-square-submatrices-with-all-ones",
  "slug": "count-square-submatrices-with-all-ones",
  "title": "Count Square Submatrices with All Ones",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "grid",
    "matrix"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "this is closely related to finding the single largest square of 1s - what does the largest-square-ending-here value at a cell actually tell you about how many total squares end at that cell?",
    "define dp[i][j] as the side length of the largest all-1s square whose bottom-right corner is cell (i, j), same as in the maximal square problem",
    "if matrix[i][j] == 1, dp[i][j] = 1 + min(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1], dp[i-1][j-1]); if matrix[i][j] == 0, dp[i][j] = 0",
    "here's the key insight: if dp[i][j] = k, that means there are exactly k distinct squares (of sizes 1x1, 2x2, ..., kxk) that all end with their bottom-right corner at (i, j)",
    "so instead of just tracking the maximum dp value, sum up every dp[i][j] across the whole table - that sum is the total count of square submatrices of all sizes containing only 1s"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "computing the same dp table as maximal square but returning the max value squared instead of the sum of all dp values",
    "forgetting that each dp[i][j] value of k represents k separate squares, not just one",
    "not handling the first row/column edge case when dp[i-1][j-1] would be out of bounds"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a `matrix` of 0s and 1s.\n\n**Count the total number of square submatrices, of any size, with all four sides aligned to the grid, that contain only 1s.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= rows, cols <= 300",
      "matrix[i][j] is either 0 or 1"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a matrix of all zeros (answer is 0)",
      "a matrix of all ones (many squares of every size up to min(rows, cols))",
      "a single row or single column (only 1x1 squares are possible)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "matrix = [[0,1,1,1],[1,1,1,1],[0,1,1,1]]",
        "output": "15",
        "expectedOutput": "15",
        "explanation": "There are 10 squares of size 1x1, 4 of size 2x2, and 1 of size 3x3, totaling 15."
      },
      {
